.TH "PKGCATALOG_COLLECTION_LAYOUT" "5" "" "libpkgcatalog\-acquire 3.0.1" "libpkgcatalog\-acquire"
.SH NAME
pkgcatalog_collection_layout \- native collection acquisition layout version 1
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
collection\-root/
├── profiles.yml
└── package\-directory/
    └── recipe.yml
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A version\-one collection root contains one optional \f[CR]profiles.yml\f[R] and immediate visible package directories.
Every such directory contains one required regular, non\-symlink \f[CR]recipe.yml\f[R].
.PP
Immediate hidden entries are ignored.
Visible symbolic links and unsupported file types are refused.
Visible regular root files other than \f[CR]profiles.yml\f[R] are ignored.
The root itself must contain no symbolic\-link component.
.PP
The package directory name is diagnostic only.
The sealed \f[CR]package.name\f[R] in the recipe is package identity.
Package\-local files are not traversed or verified by catalog acquisition.
.SH TWO\-PASS RULE
All configured \f[CR]profiles.yml\f[R] documents are parsed before any recipe is sealed.
Their declarations form one global profile namespace.
Profiles do not shadow by collection precedence.
.SH STABILITY
Callers must provide quiescent roots for one acquisition.
The adapter detects common size\-changing reads but does not create a filesystem snapshot.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The layout does not define Pkgfiles, \f[CR]pkgman.conf\f[R], Git branches, collection discovery, architecture fallback, requirement resolution, or installed state.
Translation belongs in a separate migration or configuration frontend.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]pkgcatalog_acquire(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgcatalog\-scan(1)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_profiles_yaml(5)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_recipe_yaml(5)\f[R]
